people actually had AOL,

00:11:27.258 --> 00:11:30.550
I remember thinking with Amazon,

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:33.000
hey bookstores, it's your turn, right?

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.023
And then Uber came along and it was

00:11:35.023 --> 00:11:37.771
taxi cabs, it's your turn.

00:11:37.771 --> 00:11:39.118
You know, to me,

00:11:39.118 --> 00:11:41.320
everybody is gonna have a turn

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:43.770
outside of, that is black and white.

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:45.985
I think what Common is referring to

00:11:45.985 --> 00:11:48.710
which is so powerful about art

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:50.170
is that it's gray.

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:51.329
Right?
- [Common] Yes.

00:11:51.329 --> 00:11:53.520
But I think anything
that is black and white

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:54.940
is remarkably vulnerable.

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:57.050
There's so many things that are done

00:11:57.050 --> 00:12:00.286
by people typing away at a computer.

00:12:00.286 --> 00:12:03.610
A human typing away at a computer

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:06.300
to create an action for another human

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.103
is 100 percent vulnerable.

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:10.660
- [Shahi] Phu, what about you?

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.390
